  "findings": {
    "vt_colors": "vt(4) (sys/teken) accepts 38;5;N and reduces it to 16 colors with teken_256to16; it does not implement 38;2;R;G;B and reads R, G and B as separate SGR attributes (underline, bright background via blink, reverse). The console therefore receives direct 16-color output, and tmux is told the console has 16 colors.",
    "vt_glyphs": "The default vt font (vt_font_default.c) and terminus-b32 cover the block eighths, shades, box drawing and braille used by the screen; vgarom fonts do not.",
    "vt_switch_keys": "The us vt keymap binds console switching to Alt+F1-F12 (scr01-scr12) and Print Screen (nscr/pscr) only, none of which the MacBookPro16,1 has; vidcontrol -s N works from a shell.",
    "tmux_in_closure": "tmux 3.8 is already a run dependency of the desktop closure (installed on the MacBook); adding it to the live set costs about 4 MiB with libevent and utf8proc."
  },
